---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import FlowDemo from '../components/FlowDemo.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Where Throughput Actually Stops"
  description="An interactive demonstration of maximum system flow: total throughput equals the capacity of the tightest cut, so capacity added anywhere else buys nothing."
>
  <section class="section surface-tint">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-head section-head-center">
        <p class="section-label">The idea in one graphic</p>
        <h1 class="section-title">Where throughput actually stops.</h1>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Every operation is a chain of stages, each able to carry only so much.
          Total throughput is not the average of those capacities and it is not
          the sum of them — it is whatever the tightest link will pass. Add
          capacity anywhere else and nothing happens. Move the tight link and
          the whole system moves with it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <FlowDemo />

      <div class="flow-aside">
        <h2 class="aside-title">Why this is the entire argument</h2>
        <p>
          Drag any slider and watch the number at the bottom. Most of the time
          it will not move, which is the uncomfortable part: capacity bought
          away from the constraint is capacity the system cannot use. It shows
          up as work-in-progress, not as revenue.
        </p>
        <p>
          Then press <strong>Relieve the constraint</strong>. Throughput rises —
          and the constraint immediately reappears somewhere else. That is not a
          flaw in the model. It is why a diagnostic is a repeating exercise
          rather than a one-off report, and it is what the Throughput Cycle and
          the Fractional AI Officer retainer are both built around.
        </p>
        <p class="aside-close">
          The board above uses invented numbers. Discovery runs the same
          arithmetic against yours.
        </p>
        <a href="/#discovery" class="btn btn-primary">See what Discovery covers</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .flow-aside {
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px) auto 0;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .aside-title {
    font-size: var(--step-h3);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--charcoal);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .flow-aside p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .flow-aside strong { color: var(--charcoal); }

  .aside-close {
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--terracotta);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
</style>
